<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Locke is a 60-year-old man with asthma and persistent airflow limitation on budesonide-formoterol maintenance and reliever therapy with tiotropium, who called this morning and was seen the same day. Three days ago he developed a sore throat and runny nose after a houseguest&apos;s cold; since yesterday he has had a cough, wheeze, and tightness, and woke twice last night. His home peak flow has been 290 to 310 L/min against a personal best of 440, the yellow zone of his action plan. Following the plan, he has taken five or six extra inhalations of budesonide-formoterol a day on top of his four maintenance inhalations, never more than 12 in a day, with relief for several hours each time. He has had a temperature of 37.6 C, no shaking chills, no chest pain, and no colored sputum. A home COVID-19 test yesterday was negative. He had this season&apos;s influenza, COVID-19, and RSV vaccines three weeks ago. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Cold three days ago; chest symptoms since yesterday</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Home peak flow 290 to 310 L/min (66 to 70 percent of best); woke twice last night</td></tr><tr><td>Treatment so far</td><td>Five or six extra budesonide-formoterol inhalations a day, within 12 a day; tiotropium continued</td></tr><tr><td>Pertinent negatives</td><td>No high fever, chest pain, colored sputum, or breathlessness at rest; home COVID-19 test negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

